# SCRIPT: 30_CONTEXT__Select_Property_Context
# FOLDER: 30_CONTEXT
# ROLE: set current property, resolve the correct current loan, refresh the hub
# CALLED BY: hub selector row click ; property picker change ; startup context restore
# CALLS: 10_UI__Set_Hub_Tab (conditional)
# INPUTS: $p (JSON) — { "propertyID":<req>, "loanID":<opt>, "tab":<opt> }
# GLOBALS IN: none
# RETURNS: { ok, propertyID, loanID, resolution } | { ok:false, error }
# GLOBALS OUT: g_fkCurrentProperty, g_fkCurrentLoan, optionally g_HubTab
# SIDE EFFECTS: globals only on GLOBAL_USE_VARIABLES. Creates/edits NO business records.
#
# 🥇 STATE: GOLDEN. Rewritten 2026-06-18 to kill the old `loan == property` assumption.
#   Everything else in the file depends on this resolving correctly, so it is buildOrder 4
#   (right after the txn_* trio) and it must stay thin.
#
# THE ONE THING IT EXISTS TO PREVENT:
#   Silently choosing the wrong loan. A property can have several loans — fixture PROP-001
#   has two — so when the caller does not say which, this script must either resolve
#   UNAMBIGUOUSLY or hand off to a chooser. It must never guess.
#
# PREFERRED PATH: if the selector row already knows both property and loan, PASS BOTH.
#   That skips resolution entirely and is what the live hub should do.
#
# GUARD RAILS:
#   - exit safely if no property is passed
#   - NEVER set g_fkCurrentLoan equal to the property PK (that was the old bug)
#   - never silently pick a loan when several are open
#
# ⚠️ OPEN — the multi-loan branch is a contract, not code. "Route to a controlled chooser
#   path" has no chooser behind it yet. Until one exists this script returns
#   resolution:"ambiguous" with g_fkCurrentLoan left EMPTY, and the hub must handle an
#   empty loan context rather than assuming one. An empty global is honest; a wrong one
#   is a payment posted to the wrong note.
#
# CHANGELOG:
#   - 2026-06-18 rewritten loan-aware; loanID became an optional explicit param.
#   - 2026-07-29 ported from ClickUp into a real per-script body; the ambiguous-return
#     contract made explicit so callers cannot mistake empty for resolved.

# --- SETUP ---
Set Error Capture [ On ]
Set Variable [ $p ; Value: Get ( ScriptParameter ) ]
Set Variable [ $propertyID ; Value: JSONGetElement ( $p ; "propertyID" ) ]
Set Variable [ $loanID ; Value: JSONGetElement ( $p ; "loanID" ) ]
Set Variable [ $tab ; Value: JSONGetElement ( $p ; "tab" ) ]

If [ IsEmpty ( $propertyID ) ]
	Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; False ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "error" ; "no property" ; JSONString ] ) ]
End If

# --- WRITE PROPERTY CONTEXT ---
Set Field [ GLOBAL_USE_VARIABLES::g_fkCurrentProperty ; $propertyID ]

# --- RESOLVE THE LOAN ---
If [ not IsEmpty ( $loanID ) ]
	# caller knew it. Trust it. This is the preferred path.
	Set Field [ GLOBAL_USE_VARIABLES::g_fkCurrentLoan ; $loanID ]
	Set Variable [ $resolution ; Value: "explicit" ]

Else
	# find open loans for this property
	Go to Layout [ "Loans" (Loans) ]
	Enter Find Mode [ Pause: Off ]
	Set Field [ Loans::fkProperty ; $propertyID ]
	Set Field [ Loans::ServicingStatus ; "Active" ]
	Perform Find [ ]

	If [ Get ( FoundCount ) = 1 ]
		Set Variable [ $loanID ; Value: Loans::PrimaryKey ]
		Set Field [ GLOBAL_USE_VARIABLES::g_fkCurrentLoan ; $loanID ]
		Set Variable [ $resolution ; Value: "single" ]

	Else If [ Get ( FoundCount ) = 0 ]
		# a property with no active loan is legitimate (fully paid off collateral)
		Set Field [ GLOBAL_USE_VARIABLES::g_fkCurrentLoan ; "" ]
		Set Variable [ $resolution ; Value: "none" ]

	Else
		# ⚠️ SEVERAL open loans. Do NOT guess. Leave the loan global EMPTY on purpose.
		Set Field [ GLOBAL_USE_VARIABLES::g_fkCurrentLoan ; "" ]
		Set Variable [ $resolution ; Value: "ambiguous" ]
	End If
End If

# --- CLEAR STALE ROW SELECTIONS so a tab cannot show the previous loan's row ---
Set Field [ GLOBAL_USE_VARIABLES::g_fkSelectedExpected ; "" ]
Set Field [ GLOBAL_USE_VARIABLES::g_fkSelectedTransaction ; "" ]

# --- OPTIONAL TAB LANDING ---
If [ not IsEmpty ( $tab ) ]
	Perform Script [ "10_UI__Set_Hub_Tab" ; Parameter: Param ( PText ( "tab" ; $tab ) ) ]
End If

Refresh Window [ Flush cached join results ]

Exit Script [ Result: JSONSetElement ( "{}" ; [ "ok" ; True ; JSONBoolean ] ; [ "propertyID" ; $propertyID ; JSONString ] ; [ "loanID" ; $loanID ; JSONString ] ; [ "resolution" ; $resolution ; JSONString ] ) ]

# --- FIXTURE EXPECTATION (fixtures/golden-month) ---
# PROP-001 has LOAN-001 (Active) and LOAN-003 (Paid Off) -> exactly ONE active,
#   so resolution:"single" and g_fkCurrentLoan = LOAN-001.
# PROP-002 has LOAN-002 only -> resolution:"single".
# ⚠️ NOTHING in the fixture currently produces resolution:"ambiguous". To exercise the
#   branch that matters most, flip LOAN-003 to Active and confirm the hub survives an
#   EMPTY loan context instead of silently landing on one of them.
